infection) vs empiric/targeted treatment (given when fungal infection is suspected). This study excluded because 
patients had positive Candida cultures.

3. **Study 6 (SDD trial)**: Included because amphotericin B is part of the SDD regimen providing antifungal prophylaxis,
even though the primary focus was bacterial decontamination.

4. **Study 17 (Ketoconazole for ARDS)**: Despite being an RCT with ketoconazole (an antifungal), it was excluded because
the mechanism of action studied was thromboxane inhibition, not antifungal activity, and outcomes were ARDS-related, not
fungal infection-related.

