│ azoles in high‐risk surgical intensive care unit patients: a meta‐analysis of randomized, placebo controlled         │
│ trials", "abstract": "OBJECTIVE The use of antifungal prophylaxis remains controversial in most populations          │
│ including surgical intensive care unit patients. A meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials was performed to    │
│ evaluate the safety and effectiveness of azoles as antifungal prophylaxis in high-risk patients receiving treatment  │
│ in the surgical intensive care unit. DATA SOURCE Data were obtained from PubMed, Current Contents, Cochrane central  │
│ register of controlled trials, and references from relevant articles. STUDY SELECTION Randomized controlled trials   │
