  Extended Prevalence of Infection in Intensive Care (EPIC II) study, a 1-day, prospective, point prevalence study      
  with follow-up conducted on May 8, 2007. Demographic, physiological, bacteriological, therapeutic, and outcome data   
  were collected for 14,414 patients in 1265 participating ICUs from 75 countries on the study day. Analyses focused    
  on the data from the 13,796 adult (>18 years) patients. RESULTS On the day of the study, 7087 of 13,796 patients      
  (51%) were considered infected; 9084 (71%) were receiving antibiotics. The infection was of respiratory origin in     
  4503 (64%), and microbiological culture results were positive in 4947 (70%) of the infected patients; 62% of the      
