risk of hospital mortality.                                 Conclusions.           \u2003The risk of death is           
exceptionally high among patients with septic shock attributed to Candida infection. Efforts aimed at timely source     
control and antifungal treatment are likely to be associated with improved clinical outcomes.Oxford University          
